findings.remediation:
Add a server_side_encryption_configuration block:
resource "aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration" "this" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.this.id
  rule {
    apply_server_side_encryption_by_default {
      sse_algorithm = "AES256"  # or "aws:kms" with kms_master_key_id
    }
    bucket_key_enabled = true
  }
}

Set a SAS expiry policy on the storage account so shared access signatures
cannot be minted without an expiration:
resource "azurerm_storage_account" "this" {
  # ...
  sas_policy {
    expiration_period = "00.01:00:00"
    expiration_action = "Log"
  }
}
